WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.979
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:09.222
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.522 --> 00:00:15.216
Unit nineteen: Mental Health Awareness. Today you will reassure people with 'It's okay to…'.

4
00:00:15.516 --> 00:00:18.030
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.967 --> 00:00:21.944
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.783 --> 00:00:23.773
Mental health.

7
00:00:24.783 --> 00:00:27.909
Mental health means the health of your mind and feelings.

8
00:00:28.517 --> 00:00:31.259
Mental health is as important as physical health.

9
00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:34.386
Your turn. Say: Mental health.

10
00:00:37.233 --> 00:00:38.362
Mental health.

11
00:00:39.117 --> 00:00:40.280
Awareness.

12
00:00:41.283 --> 00:00:43.515
Awareness means knowing about something.

13
00:00:44.117 --> 00:00:46.197
We held an awareness day at school.

14
00:00:46.783 --> 00:00:49.819
Your turn. Say: Awareness.

15
00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:53.819
Awareness.

16
00:00:54.583 --> 00:00:55.515
Stress.

17
00:00:56.517 --> 00:00:59.132
Stress means a feeling of pressure and worry.

18
00:00:59.717 --> 00:01:02.169
Exams cause stress for many students.

19
00:01:02.783 --> 00:01:05.470
Your turn. Say: Stress.

20
00:01:08.333 --> 00:01:09.369
Stress.

21
00:01:10.117 --> 00:01:11.524
Support system.

22
00:01:12.517 --> 00:01:14.923
Support system means people who help you.

23
00:01:15.517 --> 00:01:17.574
My friends are my support system.

24
00:01:18.183 --> 00:01:21.347
Your turn. Say: Support system.

25
00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:25.538
Support system.

26
00:01:26.283 --> 00:01:27.284
Wellbeing.

27
00:01:28.283 --> 00:01:30.817
Wellbeing means feeling healthy and happy.

28
00:01:31.417 --> 00:01:33.265
Sleep is important for wellbeing.

29
00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:36.769
Your turn. Say: Wellbeing.

30
00:01:39.633 --> 00:01:40.565
Wellbeing.

31
00:01:41.317 --> 00:01:41.969
Cope.

32
00:01:42.983 --> 00:01:45.738
Cope means to deal with a difficult situation.

33
00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:48.431
Music helps me cope with stress.

34
00:01:49.017 --> 00:01:50.810
Your turn. Say: Cope.

35
00:01:53.667 --> 00:01:54.319
Cope.

36
00:01:55.083 --> 00:01:56.038
Seek help.

37
00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:59.038
Seek help means to ask for help.

38
00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:00.976
It's brave to seek help.

39
00:02:01.583 --> 00:02:04.015
Your turn. Say: Seek help.

40
00:02:06.867 --> 00:02:07.914
Seek help.

41
00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:09.639
Balance.

42
00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:13.439
Balance means a healthy mix of work and rest.

43
00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:16.967
I try to keep a balance between study and sport.

44
00:02:17.583 --> 00:02:19.992
Your turn. Say: Balance.

45
00:02:22.833 --> 00:02:23.800
Balance.

46
00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:28.088
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:32.183
Visal, you look tired. Are you okay?

48
00:02:33.283 --> 00:02:36.354
I'm stressed about exams. Is it normal?

49
00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:41.800
Yes. It's okay to feel stressed. It's okay to seek help.

50
00:02:42.917 --> 00:02:45.221
Thank you. Who can I talk to?

51
00:02:46.317 --> 00:02:50.104
Your support system: family, friends or the school counsellor.

52
00:02:51.217 --> 00:02:55.111
I'll talk to my mum tonight. It's okay to talk about stress.

53
00:02:56.267 --> 00:02:57.837
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:58.683 --> 00:03:01.496
Grammar focus: It's okay to plus verb.

55
00:03:01.796 --> 00:03:03.064
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.262
It's okay to seek help.

57
00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:08.138
It's okay to talk about stress.

58
00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:10.864
It's okay not to be perfect.

59
00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:17.041
Use 'It's okay to' + base verb to comfort someone. For the negative, say 'It's okay not to…'.

60
00:03:17.783 --> 00:03:21.109
Be careful! Don't say: It's okay to seeking help.

61
00:03:23.067 --> 00:03:25.252
Say: It's okay to seek help.

62
00:03:25.552 --> 00:03:27.900
After 'to', use the base verb.

63
00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:31.341
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:32.133 --> 00:03:33.355
Talking Helps.

65
00:03:33.655 --> 00:03:36.131
Mental health is part of our wellbeing.

66
00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:40.062
Many students feel stress, and that is normal.

67
00:03:41.067 --> 00:03:43.182
It's okay to talk about your feelings.

68
00:03:44.167 --> 00:03:46.189
A support system helps you cope.

69
00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:50.268
It's okay to seek help and keep a healthy balance.

70
00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:55.008
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:57.652
It's okay blank seek help.

72
00:03:57.952 --> 00:04:01.130
A, to. B, for. C, that.

73
00:04:04.667 --> 00:04:06.318
The answer is A: to.

74
00:04:07.483 --> 00:04:09.866
People who help you are your support blank.

75
00:04:10.166 --> 00:04:14.052
A, system. B, balance. C, stress.

76
00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:19.530
The answer is A: system.

77
00:04:20.683 --> 00:04:23.345
To deal with a difficult situation is to blank.

78
00:04:23.645 --> 00:04:26.764
A, cope. B, seek. C, balance.

79
00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:31.754
The answer is A: cope.

80
00:04:32.967 --> 00:04:36.420
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:37.283 --> 00:04:40.537
Why is it important to talk openly about mental health?

82
00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:50.966
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:51.266 --> 00:04:58.992
It is important because many people feel alone. When we talk openly, they learn that it's okay to ask for help.

84
00:04:59.292 --> 00:05:01.129
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:02.017 --> 00:05:06.120
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and it's okay to plus verb.

86
00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:09.816
Today's value is empathy. Think about how others feel.

87
00:05:10.116 --> 00:05:12.454
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

88
00:05:12.754 --> 00:05:15.418
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

